#showas:拒绝仿冒
A somewhat more difficult Spire focused scenario. Still mainly you and the AI, and it's set to difficulty 8.
This difficulty is good for someone who is reasonably skilled at AI War 2 and wants to try a Spire setup that's a bit harder than Friends Arise.

This is on the "Clusters" map type, with 80 planets. Your main enemy is 2 Difficulty 8 AI's of the Spire Hammer type, which use cheap knock-offs of Spire craft. However, cheap knock-offs of Spire craft can still be quite powerful, especially with the main speciality of all AI's: Greater numbers. It also fortifies many of it's planets with fortresses boosted by Spire technology.

Your starting fleet is set to "Giantslayer," which is suited to helping you kill these Spire knockoffs, but might struggle more against their strikecraft in the early game.
Your battlestations are also chosen to be effective against Spire units, and your Overloader factory's speed boost can help a lot with relic retrieval missions.
This galaxy lacks officers, but that's okay: You can rely on Spire ships for that role.

Irritated by all these Spire pretenders, the Dark Spire may lash out, absorbing large amounts of energy from the Spire-scale fleet battles to warp in large forces of their own. Crush them, and the AI. There can be only one true Spire.

Hint: You may wish to choose a starting location you can easily defend.